# todo.aide — scaffoldCommands

Audit against `src/tools/init/scaffoldCommands/.aide`. The spec's target
state is "five slash command files scaffolded, each a byte-faithful
render of a canonical template read from docs/ through initContent".
The current implementation calls `getCommands()` from initContent,
which returns a map of hand-written literals; the canonical templates
do not exist under `docs/` at all yet. The first item below is a
prerequisite for this spec to be honorable by any downstream fix.

Fix agents: work one item per session. Items are sequenced — do them
in order. Do not skip ahead.

## Issues

- [x] **docs/commands/** (does not exist) — create the canonical home
      for the five pipeline slash command templates. Extract each
      template verbatim from the current `initContent.getCommands()`
      return value, one Markdown file per command:
      `docs/commands/aide-research.md`, `docs/commands/aide-spec.md`,
      `docs/commands/aide-build.md`, `docs/commands/aide-qa.md`,
      `docs/commands/aide-fix.md`. Also add `docs/commands/.aide`
      governing the subfolder as the canonical home of pipeline
      command templates — intent-form, decision-form, cascades from
      `docs/.aide`. This is the prerequisite for every other item in
      this file and for the `scaffoldCommands` spec to be honorable
      at all. Violates `outcomes.desired` #2 ("byte-faithful render
      of canonical template read from docs/").

- [ ] **src/tools/init/scaffoldCommands/index.ts** — after
      `docs/commands/` exists and `initContent` has been refactored
      (see `initContent/todo.aide`), switch this helper to request
      the five templates by canonical name from the new disk-backed
      interface. The fixed list of five names stays in this file;
      the source of each template body moves to `docs/commands/`.
      The idempotency check (`fileExists` per target path) stays
      unchanged. Violates `outcomes.desired` #2 until the switch
      lands.

- [ ] **src/tools/init/scaffoldCommands/index.ts** — confirm the
      post-refactor behavior still reports per-command statuses
      (`created` / `exists`) independently, and that a missing
      canonical template for one command surfaces as one failed
      command rather than an aborted step. The current
      implementation reads all commands from an in-memory map, so
      there is no partial-failure path today; once reads happen at
      disk-access time, the error surface grows and must not
      cascade. Violates `outcomes.undesired` #4 ("a run that fails
      the whole step if one command template is missing") if a
      cascade is introduced during the fix.

- [ ] **src/tools/init/** (cross-cutting test) — add a regression
      test that fails if any AIDE doctrine string appears as a
      literal inside `writeMethodology/index.ts`,
      `scaffoldCommands/index.ts`, or `initContent/index.ts`
      outside a trivial framework wrapper. The exact matcher is a
      fix-agent call — a reasonable starting point is "no string
      literal longer than 200 characters containing the word
      'AIDE', '.aide', or 'pipeline'". This is the permanent guard
      against reintroducing the failure mode the three helper
      specs all name. The test lives under
      `src/tools/init/` (not inside any single helper) because
      the invariant is cross-cutting.
